    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Migrate CreateEventWizard's eventService.createEvent off its ad-hoc matter/project-only map onto the ADR-024 applyResolverFields (entity-specific lookup + ALL resolver fields, 5 incl. sprk_regardingrecordnumber). Add lockAssociation support so Visual Host can hide the Associate-To step. Copy the pattern from the canonical workAssignmentService.ts.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE shared-UI developer + ADR-024 expert. Follow ADR-024 exactly (amended by #549).</role>
  <goal>eventService.createEvent writes the entity-specific @odata.bind AND all resolver fields via applyResolverFields; existing Event creation surfaces still link correctly (regression-verified); CreateRecordWizard/AssociateToStep honor a lockAssociation flag that hides/locks step 1.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>eventService currently uses a hardcoded matter/project map and SKIPS the 4 resolver fields (design §5.6, R2) — an ADR-024 violation. This is a correctness fix, not a new deviation. The canonical compliant reference is workAssignmentService.ts (nav-prop discovery → payload → BU defaults → applyResolverFields → createRecord → file pipeline → warnings). ADR-024 MUST: populate ALL resolver fields; only ONE entity-specific lookup at a time (satisfied on create-from-host); use sprk_recordtype_ref discriminator.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateEventWizard/eventService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/workAssignmentService.ts (CANONICAL — copy this pattern)
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/AssociateToStep/AssociateToStep.tsx
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateRecordWizard/CreateRecordWizard.tsx
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      .claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md
      .claude/patterns/dataverse/polymorphic-resolver.md
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateWorkAssignmentWizard/workAssignmentService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/PolymorphicResolverService.ts
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateEventWizard/eventService.ts
      projects/visual-host-create-button-r1/design.md
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step>Study workAssignmentService.ts as the canonical ADR-024 flow. Note _discoverNavProps + applyResolverFields usage and the post-#549 result type.</step>
    <step>Replace eventService.createEvent's ad-hoc regarding map with: discover sprk_event nav-props, then call applyResolverFields(webApi, entity, navProps, parentEntity, parentEntitySet, parentRecordId, parentRecordName, hint) before createRecord.</step>
    <step>Ensure all resolver fields (recordtype→sprk_recordtype_ref, recordid, recordname, recordurl, recordnumber) are written; verify sprk_recordtype_ref rows exist for the parent types.</step>
    <step>Add lockAssociation support: when true, CreateRecordWizard/AssociateToStep hides/locks step 1 and treats initialAssociation as fixed (design §5.5).</step>
    <step>Regression-test: create an Event from every existing surface (subgrid, form) and confirm the entity-specific lookup + resolver fields are set and the record opens correctly.</step>
    <step>Update/add unit tests per ADR-038.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit, Skill(adr-check), Skill(code-review)</tools>
  <outputs>Migrated eventService.ts; lockAssociation wiring in CreateRecordWizard/AssociateToStep; tests.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Created Event has one entity-specific lookup + ALL resolver fields populated (verify in Dataverse).</criterion>
    <criterion>Events created from existing surfaces still link correctly (no regression).</criterion>
    <criterion>lockAssociation=true hides step 1; false leaves it visible.</criterion>
    <criterion>adr-check passes for ADR-024; code-review clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Completed 2026-07-08 (opus-tier, FULL rigor). ADR-024 migration of shipped non-compliant code.

    ## What changed (files)
    - **eventService.ts** (`components/CreateEventWizard/`): replaced the ad-hoc matter/project-only
      regarding map (+ questionable hardcoded `fallbackMap` bind) with the canonical ADR-024 flow —
      `applyResolverFields(polyWebApi, entity, navProps, regardingEntityName, entitySet, regardingRecordId,
      regardingRecordName, hint)` before `createRecord('sprk_event', entity)`. Copied the pattern from
      `workAssignmentService.ts`. Now writes the entity-specific `@odata.bind` AND all 5 resolver fields
      (`sprk_regardingrecordtype`/`id`/`name`/`url`/`number`, post-#549). Added two small pure helpers
      `_resolveEntitySet` (logical-name → entity-set map + `${name}s` fallback; covers matter/project/
      invoice/workassignment/budget/analysis/account/contact) and `_resolveLookupHint` (strips `sprk_`
      for findNavProp disambiguation). Existing BU-cascade + event-type + AI-index binding logic untouched.
    - **AssociateToStep.tsx + types.ts**: added `locked?: boolean` prop — read-only render of the fixed
      association (no dropdown / Select / Clear); header still shown; distinct from transient `disabled`.
    - **CreateRecordWizard.tsx + types.ts**: added `lockAssociation?: boolean` to `IAssociateToStepConfig`.
      When true, the Associate-To step is REMOVED from the sequence (not merely disabled); the seeded
      `initialAssociation` still reaches `onFinish` via the existing reset-effect + `associationRef`.
      Default false = step visible/skip-able exactly as before.
    - **Tests (ADR-038-compliant — assert on real payloads/DOM; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;,
      no DI-registration, no ctor-null-check):**
      - NEW `__tests__/eventService.resolver.test.ts` (4 tests): entity-lookup + all 5 resolver fields for
        Matter; mutual exclusion (only one entity-specific lookup); no-regarding case writes nothing; NFR-06
        graceful degradation (missing catalog → still links + name fallback, skips number/type, no throw).
      - NEW `CreateRecordWizard/__tests__/CreateRecordWizard.lockAssociation.test.tsx` (2 tests): step shown
        when false, hidden when true (asserts against rendered wizard stepper).
      - EXTENDED `AssociateToStep.test.tsx` with a "locked mode" block (3 tests).

    ## Regression findings (traced every shared EventService.createEvent caller)
    - `CreateEventWizard.onFinish` → `createEvent(formValues)` with NO regarding arg → unchanged (resolver
      path not taken). Note: wiring the wizard's `context.association`/`initialAssociation` into createEvent
      is task 015's job (this task deliberately did NOT touch CreateEventWizard.tsx — not in relevant-files).
    - `CreateMatterWizard` "Create Event" follow-on → `createEvent({...regardingRecordId:matterId,
      regardingRecordName:matterName}, 'sprk_matter')` → now ADDITIVELY writes the 5 resolver fields on top
      of the Matter lookup. No throw path (graceful-blank). Strict correctness upgrade.
    - `CreateProjectWizard` "Create Event" follow-on → same, `'sprk_project'`. Correctness upgrade.
    - Existing `eventService.cascade.test.ts` (7 tests incl. one with `regardingRecordId`+`'sprk_matter'`):
      STILL GREEN — BU-cascade payload unaffected; resolver degrades cleanly on the empty mock.
    Conclusion: no existing surface loses its link; Matter/Project follow-on events upgrade lookup-only →
    full ADR-024. No functional regression.

    ## Behavioral note (intentional, low risk)
    Old code had a hardcoded metadata fallback (`sprk_regardingmatterid_sprk_matter@odata.bind`) when
    nav-prop discovery returned nothing. New `applyResolverFields` warns + skips the entity-specific lookup
    instead (ADR-024-correct, matches workAssignmentService). Nav-prop discovery is the same mechanism
    already trusted for event-type/AI-index binds in this method, so real-world impact is nil.

    ## Quality gates (UNCONDITIONAL for this task)
    - typecheck (`tsc --noEmit`): clean. ESLint (modified files): clean. Tests: 50/50 green across the 4
      affected suites.
    - **adr-check**: 0 violations. ADR-024/012/021 compliant. This change REMOVES a shipped ADR-024
      violation (design §5.6/R2) — no §6.5 escalation needed. One informational warning: extend
      `_ENTITY_SET_MAP` when future irregular-plural Event host types are wired.
    - **code-review**: Approve. 0 critical / 0 warning. Clean on all 5 AI-code-smell dimensions. Regression
      assessment: no regression across all three Event-creation surfaces.

    ## Follow-ups for downstream tasks (not blockers)
    - Task 015 wires the `event` registry key and should pass the host `context.association`/
      `initialAssociation` into `eventService.createEvent` (deriving `regardingEntityName` from
      `association.entityType`, seeding `regardingRecordId`/`Name`) so the resolver is exercised end-to-end
      from Visual Host, and configure `associateToStep` with `lockAssociation: true` when launched from a visual.
    - No ADR conflict requiring human sign-off surfaced.
  </notes>
</task>
